/-!
# The ATLAS permutation model of the McLaughlin group

`TauCeti.Sporadic.McL` is the subgroup of permutations of `Fin 275` generated by the
literal forward images in the ATLAS files `McLG1-p275B0.m1` and `McLG1-p275B0.m2`.
The file points `1, …, 275` become `0, …, 274`. The inverse image table for the second
generator is included so that both directions compute without a search.

Sending the two generators of the transcribed presentation to `McL.a⁻¹` and `McL.b⁻¹`
satisfies all fifteen relators. Inversion corrects the source's left-to-right composition
to Mathlib's right-to-left composition. The assigned permutations generate exactly `McL`,
so `exists_surjective_McL` gives a surjection from the presented group onto this model.
In particular both groups are nontrivial. No order or simplicity assertion is made here.

The lift and range arguments use `GroupPresentation.homEquiv` and
`GroupPresentation.exists_surjective_of_closure_range_eq`.

## References

* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, representation `McLG1-p275B0` and Bray's presentation `McLG1-P1`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/>. The image data are from
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/McL/mtx/McLG1-p275B0.m1> and
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/McL/mtx/McLG1-p275B0.m2>.
-/

public section

open scoped commutatorElement

